%% alt: A release loop. A change to a prompt, a model or a retrieval step runs the offline evals: the test set graded by code checks, a calibrated model judge and human review. A release gate then compares every slice with the current version. A regression sends the change back to be fixed. A pass goes to a canary on a share of live traffic, watched by online evals, which can roll it back; otherwise it rolls out to everyone. Failures found in production become new test cases.
%% caption: Every change passes the same gate, and every failure found in production becomes a new test case.
flowchart TB
  classDef control fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#1f1147
  classDef data fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#b45309,color:#3b2405

  change(["A change: prompt,<br/>model or retrieval"])
  offline["Offline evals<br/>code checks · judge · people"]
  gate{{"Release gate:<br/>no slice regresses"}}:::control
  canary["Canary,<br/>with online evals"]
  live(["Full rollout"])
  tests[("Test set")]:::data

  change --> offline --> gate
  gate -- "pass" --> canary --> live
  gate -. "regression: fix it" .-> change
  canary -. "roll back" .-> change
  live -. "new failures" .-> tests
  tests --> offline
